WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.284 --> 00:00:19.826
yelled, rushing after Nora as she tiptoed across their yard.

2
00:00:19.846 --> 00:00:21.667
"What are you doing?

3
00:00:22.788 --> 00:00:24.429
Why'd you climb out that window?"

4
00:00:24.449 --> 00:00:27.631
"Come on," Henry said to Cole and Maggie.

5
00:00:27.651 --> 00:00:29.632
"Let's catch up to them."

6
00:00:30.784 --> 00:00:34.245
The Lemonade Detectives ran across the yard after Nathan.

7
00:00:35.105 --> 00:00:38.346
By the time they reached him, Nora had stopped and spun around.

8
00:00:39.707 --> 00:00:41.107
She glared at her brother.

9
00:00:41.127 --> 00:00:43.948
"It's none of your business!"

10
00:00:44.368 --> 00:00:45.228
she yelled at him.

11
00:00:45.248 --> 00:00:47.029
"Where were you going?"

12
00:00:47.969 --> 00:00:50.650
Cole asked Nora, glancing around the yard.

13
00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:52.951
Henry looked around too.

14
00:00:53.991 --> 00:00:56.352
Nathan and Nora's backyard was really nice.

15
00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:01.743
There was a big maple tree in the middle where Nathan and his dad had built a tree

16
00:01:01.784 --> 00:01:07.348
house. On the left there was a short picket fence between their yard and the one next door.

17
00:01:08.329 --> 00:01:11.712
A tall hedge on the right blocked the view of the other neighbors' house.

18
00:01:12.733 --> 00:01:16.516
There were no neighbors at all at the back of the yard, just a thick forest.

19
00:01:17.557 --> 00:01:20.860
Henry was pretty sure Nora was headed there when they'd caught her.

20
00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.602
"Yeah," he said.

21
00:01:23.622 --> 00:01:25.924
"Where were you going, Nora?"

22
00:01:26.856 --> 00:01:29.639
Nora stared at Henry, then at each of the others.

23
00:01:30.679 --> 00:01:31.901
She looked suspicious.

24
00:01:31.921 --> 00:01:34.082
"Who wants to know?"

25
00:01:34.102 --> 00:01:38.446
"The Lemonade Detectives, that's who," Maggie replied.

26
00:01:38.466 --> 00:01:40.848
"We want to know what you're up to!"

27
00:01:41.889 --> 00:01:42.790
Henry winced.

28
00:01:44.591 --> 00:01:48.815
He didn't think it was a very good idea to tell Nora that they were investigating her.

29
00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:51.357
But Maggie was impulsive.

30
00:01:52.478 --> 00:01:54.160
She often spoke before she thought.

31
00:01:55.136 --> 00:01:56.577
Nora stared at them all again.

32
00:01:57.518 --> 00:01:59.179
For a second she didn't answer.

33
00:01:59.199 --> 00:02:01.941
"Well?" Nathan demanded.

34
00:02:01.961 --> 00:02:06.504
"I was just walking across the backyard," Nora said at last.

35
00:02:06.524 --> 00:02:09.106
"What's wrong with that?"

36
00:02:10.027 --> 00:02:13.249
"Why did you climb out the playroom window instead of using the door?"

37
00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:16.591
Nathan pointed to the back door of their house.

38
00:02:16.611 --> 00:02:19.013
"It's right there, you know!"

39
00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:21.935
"I was in a hurry," Nora said.

40
00:02:21.955 --> 00:02:25.946
"I, um, saw a butterfly and I wanted to catch it."

41
00:02:27.487 --> 00:02:28.768
Henry glanced at Cole.

42
00:02:29.628 --> 00:02:32.570
He could tell his friend was thinking the same thing he was.

43
00:02:33.611 --> 00:02:34.692
Nora was lying.

44
00:02:35.673 --> 00:02:38.295
But how were they supposed to get her to tell the truth now?

45
00:02:39.435 --> 00:02:40.936
She knew they were watching her.

46
00:02:41.837 --> 00:02:44.999
That was going to make their job as detectives much harder.

47
00:02:45.019 --> 00:02:47.881
"It's okay, Nora," Henry said.

48
00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:51.164
"Go ahead and do whatever you were doing."

49
00:02:52.116 --> 00:02:54.458
"I wasn't doing anything," Nora said.

50
00:02:54.478 --> 00:02:57.520
"I was just about to go back inside."

51
00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:01.302
She ran over and climbed back inside through the window.

52
00:03:02.403 --> 00:03:03.744
Maggie stared after her.

53
00:03:03.764 --> 00:03:06.806
"You were right," she told Nathan.

54
00:03:08.287 --> 00:03:11.289
"She is acting even weirder than usual."

55
00:03:12.329 --> 00:03:13.170
Cole shrugged.

56
00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:14.991
"So what do we do now?

57
00:03:16.012 --> 00:03:18.013
She didn't seem very eager to tell us anything."

58
00:03:19.174 --> 00:03:22.956
"We'll have to figure out what's going on in a different way," Henry said.

59
00:03:22.976 --> 00:03:27.197
"Maybe we should try a stakeout," Maggie suggested.

60
00:03:27.217 --> 00:03:30.838
"That worked last time we were suspicious of her."

61
00:03:31.919 --> 00:03:33.559
"No it didn't," Cole said.

62
00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:37.100
"Last time we staked out Nora's house, she turned out to be innocent."

63
00:03:37.981 --> 00:03:41.001
"True, but Maggie's right," Henry said.

64
00:03:41.021 --> 00:03:46.243
"If we hide and wait for Nora to sneak out again, we'll be able to follow her.

65
00:03:47.243 --> 00:03:49.684
Then we can see where she's going and what she's doing."

66
00:03:50.948 --> 00:03:53.809
"You mean we have to sit around here all day?"

67
00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:58.251
Maggie suddenly didn't look very happy about the stakeout idea.

68
00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:00.812
"What about my lemonade stand?"

69
00:04:01.873 --> 00:04:03.133
Henry glanced at Nathan.

70
00:04:03.153 --> 00:04:06.855
"You said she's been sneaking out at night, right?"

71
00:04:06.875 --> 00:04:09.396
"Sort of," Nathan said.

72
00:04:09.416 --> 00:04:14.999
"Her bedtime is at seven, so it's not usually very late when she sneaks out."

73
00:04:16.159 --> 00:04:17.820
"Perfect." Henry smiled.

74
00:04:18.836 --> 00:04:21.398
"All we have to do is come back at seven and wait!"

75
00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:29.486
That evening at exactly seven o'clock, The Lemonade Detectives met behind the hedge along Nora's yard.

76
00:04:30.947 --> 00:04:32.528
Nathan was waiting for them there.

77
00:04:32.548 --> 00:04:35.471
"Perfect timing," he whispered.

78
00:04:35.491 --> 00:04:37.713
"Nora just went to bed."

79
00:04:38.754 --> 00:04:39.534
Henry nodded.

80
00:04:40.435 --> 00:04:41.516
He peeked through the hedge.

81
00:04:42.617 --> 00:04:45.580
It hid them from view, but allowed them to see Nora's house.

82
00:04:46.624 --> 00:04:48.906
"Does she usually sneak out the back door?"

83
00:04:49.246 --> 00:04:49.767
he asked.

84
00:04:49.787 --> 00:04:53.049
"She used to," Nathan replied.

85
00:04:53.069 --> 00:04:56.993
"But Mom and Dad started locking it once all this started."

86
00:04:57.013 --> 00:05:01.236
"Maybe she'll climb out the playroom window again," Cole said.

87
00:05:02.257 --> 00:05:03.097
Nathan nodded.

88
00:05:03.117 --> 00:05:06.460
"Or she might use her bedroom window," he said.

89
00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:10.503
"It's upstairs, but she knows how to climb down the house.

90
00:05:12.065 --> 00:05:14.186
It's part of our family's fire-safety plan."

91
00:05:16.064 --> 00:05:18.725
"Okay, let's watch both windows," Henry said.

92
00:05:19.685 --> 00:05:22.086
They all settled down behind the hedge to wait.

93
00:05:23.086 --> 00:05:24.706
But they didn't have to wait very long.

94
00:05:25.747 --> 00:05:29.208
About twenty minutes later, they heard a window slide open.

95
00:05:30.168 --> 00:05:31.508
Maggie peeked through the hedge.

96
00:05:31.528 --> 00:05:33.549
"It's Nora!"

97
00:05:33.869 --> 00:05:34.489
she whispered.

98
00:05:34.509 --> 00:05:38.390
"She's climbing out her bedroom window."

99
00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:40.311
Henry looked too.

100
00:05:41.311 --> 00:05:44.712
He saw Nora climb out her bedroom window and jump to the ground.

101
00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:48.884
She glanced around, and then scurried across the yard.

102
00:05:48.904 --> 00:05:53.589
"She sure doesn't look like she's sleepwalking," Henry whispered.

103
00:05:53.609 --> 00:05:56.092
"Come on, let's follow her!"
